  "plan_source": "task 035",
  "sheet_prompt": "One illustration of 4 separate characters arranged in 2 rows of 2, evenly spaced across a single seamless background.\nSubject: a bold red caped figure with a yellow emblem on the chest.\nStyle: soft 3D clay render, chunky rounded forms, matte material, gentle studio lighting, charming handmade feel.\nOutline: none. Draw every character directly on the background with no outline, border, stroke, die-cut edge or halo around it.\nReading left to right, top to bottom, every character is a different moment: a wide range of emotions AND different states of action (standing, walking, running, jumping, sitting, lying down, leaning, reaching, spinning), so no two characters share a pose, a body position or a silhouette:\nCharacter 1: standing tall with arms crossed in proud victory pose\nCharacter 2: jumping high with cape flowing behind in pure joy\nCharacter 3: leaning forward with hands clasped in deep concern\nCharacter 4: falling to knees with head down in total defeat\nMake every expression big and readable at small size: exaggerated eyes, eyebrows, mouth and body language.\nConsistency: the same character design, proportions and colours for all 4 characters.\nBackground: a single, seamless, solid pure green (#00FF00) background covering the whole image in exactly one shade, with no tiled panels, no shading variations, no tint, gradient, vignette or glow, no shadows, no floor, no noise.\nSpacing: every character is full body with a generous empty margin on every side (at least 20% of its own size), clearly separated from the others, none touching or crossing another.",
  "video_prompt": "Animate this illustration sheet as a 3-second clip. Every character performs its own big, highly expressive, cartoon-style animation in place, inside its own cell, showing a wide range of emotions:\n1. swaying slightly while keeping feet planted firmly together\n2. mid-air leap before landing softly on both feet\n3. twitching shoulders while leaning heavily on one leg\n4. dropping low to the ground and sliding forward slowly\nAnimation style: wide emotions, highly expressive faces and bodies, exaggerated squash and stretch, anticipation and follow-through, clear facial animation (eyes, eyebrows, mouth), secondary motion on ears, tails and props, each character on its own rhythm, lively and full of personality. Never a static pose and never only a gentle sway.\nKeep every character inside its own slot of the 2x2 layout; nothing may touch or cross a slot edge, and characters never interact with one another.\nEmpty slots stay empty: do not add any character, object or effect to them.\nStatic camera, no zoom, no pan, no cuts. Keep the one flat pure green (#00FF00) background exactly as it is, the same shade everywhere: no shadows, no gradient, no noise, no glow.\nKeep each character's design, proportions and colours unchanged and do not add outlines or borders.",
